.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd October 23, 2026
.Dt EFIVAR 8
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm efivar
.Nd show and change UEFI variables
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl AbgHNqRu
.Fl l
.Op Fl p
.Nm
.Op Fl AbdgHNqRu
.Op Fl Fl load-option
.Op Fl p
.Fl n Ar name | Ar name
.Nm
.Op Fl q
.Op Fl t Ar attributes
.Op Fl f Ar file
.Fl w | Fl a
.Fl n Ar name
.Nm
.Op Fl q
.Fl D
.Fl n Ar name
.Nm
.Op Fl R
.Fl L
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
lists, prints, writes and deletes the firmware's variables through
.Xr efi 4 .
A variable is named by its vendor GUID and its name,
.Ar guid Ns Li - Ns Ar name
.Pq Li 8be4df61-93ca-11d2-aa0d-00e098032b8c-BootOrder ,
or with a well-known GUID's name in place of the GUID
.Pq Li global-BootOrder .
.Pp
The options are FreeBSD's:
.Bl -tag -width "-t attributes"
.It Fl l , Fl Fl list
List every variable; with
.Fl p ,
each one's value too.
.It Fl p , Fl Fl print
Print the variable's value (the default for a name).
.It Fl n Ar name , Fl Fl name Ar name
The variable to work on; also given as the operand.
.It Fl w , Fl Fl write
Set the variable to the standard input, or to
.Ar file .
.It Fl a , Fl Fl append
Append the standard input, or
.Ar file ,
to it.
.It Fl D , Fl Fl delete
Delete it.
.It Fl f Ar file , Fl Fl fromfile Ar file
Write or append
.Ar file Ns 's
contents.
.It Fl t Ar attributes , Fl Fl attributes Ar attributes
The attributes to write with, in hex; 7 (non-volatile, at boot and at run
time) by default.
.It Fl H , Fl Fl hex
Print values as a hex dump (the default).
.It Fl A , Fl Fl ascii
Print values as text, a byte outside printable ASCII as
.Ql % Ns Ar xx .
.It Fl u , Fl Fl utf8
Print values as UCS-2 text, in UTF-8.
.It Fl b , Fl Fl binary
Print values as they are.
.It Fl d , Fl Fl device-path
Print values as UEFI device paths, in the specification's text form
.Pq Li HD(1,GPT,...,0x800,0x82000)/\eEFI\eBOOT\eBOOTX64.EFI .
.It Fl Fl load-option
Print values as boot entries
.Pq Li EFI_LOAD_OPTION :
.Ql *
if active, the label, and the device path.
.It Fl N , Fl Fl no-name
Leave out the variable's name.
.It Fl g , Fl Fl guid
Show well-known GUIDs by name.
.It Fl R , Fl Fl raw-guid
Show GUIDs as numbers.
.It Fl L , Fl Fl list-guids
List the well-known GUIDs:
.Li global ,
.Li oxidebsd ,
.Li security
and
.Li shell .
.It Fl q , Fl Fl quiet
Print no error messages.
.El
.Pp
Writing is root's, and limited to the boot manager's variables and
OxideBSD's own unless
.Va machdep.efi.unsafe_writes
is set
.Pq Xr efi 4 .
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 otherwise.
.Sh EXAMPLES
The boot order:
.Dl efivar -p global-BootOrder
.Pp
A variable of OxideBSD's own, written and read back:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
printf hello | efivar -w -n oxidebsd-Note
efivar -A -N oxidebsd-Note
.Ed
.Pp
A boot entry, decoded:
.Dl efivar --load-option global-Boot0001
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr efi 4 ,
.Xr efibootmgr 8
.Sh HISTORY
An
.Nm
first appeared in FreeBSD 11.1; OxideBSD's in OxideBSD 0.3.
